LATENT DISPATCH
Tue Sep 8 · 5 items · ~4 min

ARGENT SYSTEMS CUTS MID-TIER PRICES 25%
Argent dropped its prices on every model in the 10–35B class by a quarter, effective immediately, with no volume requirement. Kestrel and Nimbus have not matched yet. Given how August went, we would not sign an annual commit at current prices anywhere. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/argent-cut

SABLE-3 GETS AN "AGENT MODE"
Sable Labs shipped a server-side agent loop: you give it tools and a goal, it runs the loop, you get the result and a trace. It is convenient and it is lock-in; the trace format is proprietary and the loop cannot be interrupted mid-run. Fine for prototypes, think twice for production.

STRUCTURED OUTPUT BAKE-OFF
We sent 20,000 extraction prompts with a strict JSON schema to nine models. Schema-valid rate: 99.7% at the top, 96% at the bottom. The gap sounds small until you multiply by call volume. Full table and the schema we used: https://latentdispatch.ai/p/structured-bakeoff

OSTRAVA DOCUMENT MODEL NOW ON KESTREL
The Czech lab's document-understanding model is available via Kestrel at $0.003 per page. First hosted availability outside their own API.

SHORT TAKES
· Larkspur 1.1: checkpoint-and-resume across process restarts.
· Brindle open-sources its replay-log format. Good move; watch whether Larkspur adopts it.
· Quillon-M adds a "confidence per field" output. We asked for this. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/quillon-confidence

